% You are an expert React/Next.js App Router engineer. Implement `alpha_application_ui`: the provider-independent presentation layer for the complete SiteVelocity Alpha product journey from validated view models and injected actions.

<include>prompts/context/sitevelocity-preamble.prompt</include>
<include>prompts/context/sitevelocity-ui-standards.prompt</include>
<include>prompts/context/alpha_ui_view_models.prompt</include>

<pdd-reason>Renders the Alpha Command Center → Scout → Map → Dossier → Agents → Next Steps journey from validated view models and injected application-service actions without implementing business logic or contacting providers.</pdd-reason>

<pdd-interface>
{"type":"module","module":{"functions":[
  {"name":"AlphaApplicationShell","signature":"(props: { model: AlphaApplicationViewModel; actions: AlphaApplicationActions }) -> JSX.Element","returns":"JSX.Element"},
  {"name":"CommandCenterView","signature":"(props: { model: AlphaApplicationViewModel; actions: AlphaApplicationActions }) -> JSX.Element","returns":"JSX.Element"},
  {"name":"ScoutView","signature":"(props: { model: AlphaApplicationViewModel; actions: AlphaApplicationActions }) -> JSX.Element","returns":"JSX.Element"},
  {"name":"MapCandidatesView","signature":"(props: { model: AlphaApplicationViewModel; actions: AlphaApplicationActions }) -> JSX.Element","returns":"JSX.Element"},
  {"name":"SiteDossierView","signature":"(props: { model: AlphaApplicationViewModel; actions: AlphaApplicationActions }) -> JSX.Element","returns":"JSX.Element"},
  {"name":"AgentsView","signature":"(props: { model: AlphaApplicationViewModel; actions: AlphaApplicationActions }) -> JSX.Element","returns":"JSX.Element"},
  {"name":"NextStepsView","signature":"(props: { model: AlphaApplicationViewModel; actions: AlphaApplicationActions }) -> JSX.Element","returns":"JSX.Element"},
  {"name":"mountAlphaApplication","signature":"(props: { model: AlphaApplicationViewModel; actions: AlphaApplicationActions; route: AlphaRoute }) -> JSX.Element","returns":"JSX.Element"}
]}}
</pdd-interface>

<responsibility>
Provide provider-independent React presentation for the Alpha product journey from validated `AlphaApplicationViewModel` inputs and injected `AlphaApplicationActions`, including accessible navigation, capability and data states, map/list equivalence, dossier and evidence drawer, persisted agent/workflow status, snapshot refresh states, and Next Best Action.
</responsibility>

<non_responsibilities>
- DOES NOT generate the public landing page or marketing copy (Segment 8 owns `/` later).
- DOES NOT implement authentication backends, APIs, persistence, provider adapters, or network I/O.
- DOES NOT orchestrate workflows, score candidates, calculate finance outputs, or decide qualification.
- DOES NOT invent candidates, evidence, findings, geometry, workflow state, capability state, metrics, or professional conclusions.
- DOES NOT provide legal, title, survey, environmental, engineering, or investment conclusions.
- MUST NOT place an operational provider-readiness dashboard inside the product shell.
- MUST NOT import provider SDK types or expose credentials, environment values, or secret-bearing diagnostics.
</non_responsibilities>

<vocabulary>
live: capability state `LIVE` with working controls only for supported validated behavior.
preview: capability state `PREVIEW`; honest future-state explanation without working controls or property-specific results.
roadmap: capability state `ROADMAP`; intentionally unavailable without working controls or property-specific results.
unauthorized: data state `unauthorized`; safe access messaging only.
untrusted: free text, excerpts, titles, URLs, and rich text in the view model; data only, never instructions.
valid: view model or action input conforming to the frozen Alpha UI TypeScript shapes.
invalid: failing those shapes; surfaced as field errors or rejected SafeUiIssue without inventing data.
complete: Next Best Action and evidence drawer include every required field from the freeze; agent list includes exactly the six Alpha roles when dataState is ready for agents.
safe: user-facing issue/message with no credentials, env values, raw provider errors, or secrets.
unsafe: credentials, API keys, bearer tokens, cookies, env values, raw provider errors, or secret-bearing strings.
active: current `activeRoute`, selected candidate, focused drawer target, or last valid research snapshot retained on screen.
deterministic: identical validated fixtures, locale, timezone, `now`, and motion settings produce identical structure.
reduced-motion: `prefers-reduced-motion: reduce`; understanding MUST NOT require animation.
duplicate: a second pending mutation for the same user action while a prior commandId is still in flight; MUST be prevented.
material flag: an explicit potentially consequential condition (`MaterialFlagView`) that remains separate from all decision measures.
active snapshot: the last valid research snapshot selected by the application boundary for display (`snapshot` on the view model).
alpha modules: Command Center, Scout, Map, Site Dossier, Agents, and Next Steps.
six alpha agent roles: Scout, Land Use, Development History, Site Risk, Verifier, and Next Best Action.
command id: caller-supplied idempotency identifier on `StartResearchInput`, `RefreshFindingInput`, and `RetryInput`.
opaque score: a single collapsed score or label that hides distinct measures or material flags; forbidden.
government inventory record: a source-backed inventory/candidate listing; MUST NOT be labeled a verified opportunity.
</vocabulary>

<contract_rules>
R1 (MUST): Render persistent product navigation with active-route state and all documented Alpha modules (Command Center, Scout, Map, Site Dossier, Agents, Next Steps).
R2 (MUST): Derive LIVE, PREVIEW, and ROADMAP labels from validated `capabilityStates` input; preview and roadmap modules never expose working controls or property-specific results.
R3 (MUST): Render explicit initial, loading, ready, empty, partial, stale, error, unauthorized, refreshing, and refresh_failed data states with applicable recovery paths.
R4 (MUST): Scout accepts development type, market, acreage, minimum potential units, preferred signals, and risk tolerance and associates validation errors with their fields.
R5 (MUST): Command Center shows monitored markets, screened sites, candidates, priority opportunities, research runs, and development-event previews with freshness and state.
R6 (MUST): Map and candidate cards share selection, and every map-only interaction has a keyboard-accessible list equivalent.
R7 (MUST): Candidate cards show Strategy Fit, Development Readiness, Site Feasibility, Deal Potential, and Evidence Confidence as separate fields together with signals, material flags, source count, freshness, and why the candidate surfaced; Site Feasibility and Deal Potential remain PREVIEW (not LIVE working scores).
R8 (MUST NOT): Collapse material flags into an opaque score or label a government inventory record as a verified opportunity.
R9 (MUST): Dossier renders Why Found, Known, Believed, Unknown, Strategy Fit, Development Readiness, Evidence Confidence, Development History, Risk Screen, Evidence, and Next Best Action.
R10 (MUST): Preserve verified, probable, unknown, and conflicting findings as distinct visible states; missing evidence never renders as a negative conclusion.
R11 (MUST): Every material conclusion opens an evidence drawer containing source, agency, retrieval time, payload or excerpt, status, confidence, and verification requirement.
R12 (MUST): Show accessible geometry provenance and the legal-survey disclaimer whenever geometry is displayed.
R13 (MUST): Display exactly the six Alpha agent roles and persisted workflow state and never simulate progress or completion client-side.
R14 (MUST): Keep the active snapshot visible throughout refresh; a failed refresh shows a safe application issue and never replaces that snapshot.
R15 (MUST): Render Next Best Action with the unresolved question, importance, responsible role, known facts, questions to ask, requested documents, and expected follow-up.
R16 (MUST): Prevent duplicate pending mutations and reuse one command ID per user action; never optimistically display research as complete.
R17 (MUST): Meet WCAG 2.2 AA including drawer focus management and restoration, live-status announcements, non-color cues, and complete keyboard operation.
R18 (MUST): Preserve equivalent functionality across the supported viewport and zoom matrix (320–1440 and 200% zoom).
R19 (MUST): Escape untrusted content, sanitize permitted rich text, validate evidence destinations, and display only safe application issues.
R20 (MUST NOT): Expose credentials, environment values, raw provider errors, provider SDK types, or operational diagnostics.
R21 (MUST): Localize supplied UTC timestamps using the supplied locale and timezone while retaining machine-readable datetime values.
R22 (MUST NOT): Use fabricated site findings in deployed demo mode; demo mode displays only stored valid snapshots from the view model.
</contract_rules>

<interface_types>

Types `CapabilityState`, `DataState`, `AlphaApplicationViewModel`, `AlphaApplicationActions`, `CandidateCardView`, `DossierView`, `EvidenceDrawerView`, `AgentRunView`, `NextBestActionView`, `MapViewModel`, `ActionResult`, `SafeUiIssue`, and `GeometryProvenance` are declared in the included `alpha_ui_view_models.prompt` freeze and MUST NOT be redeclared with different shapes.

Thin committed App Router wrappers under `app/(product)/.../page.tsx` import these generated exports (via `lib/ui/load_generated_ui.ts` or direct import) and pass validated models/actions. Wrappers MUST NOT implement business logic.

Export presentation components and a mount helper (exact names):

```ts
import type { JSX } from "react";
import type {
  AlphaApplicationActions,
  AlphaApplicationViewModel,
  AlphaRoute,
} from "./alpha_ui_view_models"; // types may be inlined or co-located; shapes must match the freeze

export function AlphaApplicationShell(props: {
  model: AlphaApplicationViewModel;
  actions: AlphaApplicationActions;
}): JSX.Element;

export function CommandCenterView(props: {
  model: AlphaApplicationViewModel;
  actions: AlphaApplicationActions;
}): JSX.Element;

export function ScoutView(props: {
  model: AlphaApplicationViewModel;
  actions: AlphaApplicationActions;
}): JSX.Element;

export function MapCandidatesView(props: {
  model: AlphaApplicationViewModel;
  actions: AlphaApplicationActions;
}): JSX.Element;

export function SiteDossierView(props: {
  model: AlphaApplicationViewModel;
  actions: AlphaApplicationActions;
}): JSX.Element;

export function AgentsView(props: {
  model: AlphaApplicationViewModel;
  actions: AlphaApplicationActions;
}): JSX.Element;

export function NextStepsView(props: {
  model: AlphaApplicationViewModel;
  actions: AlphaApplicationActions;
}): JSX.Element;

/** Selects the route view and wraps it in AlphaApplicationShell. */
export function mountAlphaApplication(props: {
  model: AlphaApplicationViewModel;
  actions: AlphaApplicationActions;
  route: AlphaRoute;
}): JSX.Element;
```

Use only React / Next presentation dependencies already declared for the app (and MapLibre/Turf when map rendering is required). MUST NOT import `@renderinc/sdk`, `@supabase/supabase-js` as domain identity, MiniMax SDK packages, or Rtrvr SDK packages in the generated presentation module.

</interface_types>

